  "summary": "Soul revived on hip-hop's grooves, named by Kedar Massenburg after D'Angelo's Brown Sugar (1995): D'Angelo, Erykah Badu, Maxwell, Lauryn Hill, and the Soulquarians round Questlove and J Dilla at Electric Lady. Live players in place of samples, with grooves shaped at the level of milliseconds: a drummer playing loose and late against a bass that is later still.",
